## Problem

Supabase insert fails when users select custom neighborhood. The bug: `formData.neighborhoodId ? parseInt(formData.neighborhoodId) : null` evaluates `parseInt("")` → `NaN` because empty string is truthy. Database rejects `NaN` for integer column.

## Changes

**Strict normalization (26 lines)** before database insert ensures:

- `neighborhood_id`: valid integer or null (never `NaN`, never empty string)
- `custom_neighborhood`: trimmed non-empty string or null (never `""`)
- Mutual exclusivity: only one field set at a time (custom takes priority)
- DEV logging of normalized values before insert

```javascript
// Before (buggy)
neighborhood_id: formData.neighborhoodId ? parseInt(formData.neighborhoodId) : null,
custom_neighborhood: formData.customNeighborhood || null,

// After (strict normalization)
const normalizedNeighborhoodId = formData.neighborhoodId && formData.neighborhoodId.trim() !== '' 
  ? parseInt(formData.neighborhoodId, 10) 
  : null;
const normalizedCustomNeighborhood = formData.customNeighborhood && formData.customNeighborhood.trim() !== '' 
  ? formData.customNeighborhood.trim() 
  : null;

// Enforce mutual exclusivity
const finalNeighborhoodId = normalizedCustomNeighborhood ? null : normalizedNeighborhoodId;
const finalCustomNeighborhood = finalNeighborhoodId ? null : normalizedCustomNeighborhood;

// Validate no NaN edge cases
if (finalNeighborhoodId !== null && isNaN(finalNeighborhoodId)) {
  throw new Error(`Invalid neighborhood_id: '${formData.neighborhoodId}' is not a valid integer`);
}
```

**File modified:** `src/pages/AddListing.tsx` (lines 425-458)

**Approach:** Surgical fix at data preparation layer. No form refactoring.

